{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — Request Private Appointment (Wireframe 03 §05).

  Aloha, 3 September 2026, answering the open question from the last build:
    "Please make this a modal enquiry form rather than taking the customer away
     from the product page. It should automatically record the product or Style
     being viewed and request: Name, Email address, Telephone number, Preferred
     appointment date or general availability, Message."

  So this is now a modal, and the visitor never leaves the page.

  WHAT IT RECORDS AUTOMATICALLY
  Everything identifying the garment is filled in before the visitor sees the
  form, from the same metafields the rest of the page reads:

      Style          hartwick.style -> display_name   (falls back to product.title)
      Expression     hartwick.expression
      Lot            hartwick.lot -> number_roman, as a Roman numeral
      Product        product.title
      Product URL    the canonical URL, so the reply can link straight back
      Selected size  read from the live product form when the modal opens
                     (assets/ha-appointment.js) — it changes as the visitor
                     changes it, so it cannot be baked in here

  WHY A NATIVE <dialog>
  `showModal()` gives the focus trap, the Escape key, the inert background and
  the backdrop from the browser, correctly, with no library. Luxe's own
  `contact-drawer` snippet was the other candidate and was rejected: it is a
  side drawer rather than a modal, it is hard-wired to a single `#contact-drawer-link`
  in the header, and it throws if that link is absent — it is orphaned in this
  theme and nothing renders it.

  WHY THE NATIVE CONTACT FORM
  `{% form 'contact' %}` is Shopify's own. It carries the spam protection, the
  server-side validation and the delivery, and it needs no app and no third-party
  endpoint. Every extra field is sent as a labelled line in the notification.

  WHERE IT LANDS — one thing the theme genuinely cannot set. Shopify delivers
  every contact-form submission to the store's sender email
  (Settings > Notifications). It is not a theme value, so it is not settable
  here. Aloha has said she will confirm the Hartwick address; whoever sets it
  sets it there. Until then, `ha_appointment_recipient` in theme settings adds a
  "Route to" line to the body of the email so a forwarding rule can pick these
  out, and every submission is already tagged `Enquiry type: Private appointment`.

  The behaviour lives in assets/ha-appointment.js, loaded once from
  layout/theme.liquid on the product template — not from here, so the modal
  cannot ship the same script twice if it is ever rendered more than once.

  Usage (inside a main-product custom_liquid block):
    {% render 'ha-appointment', text: 'Request Private Appointment' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign label = text | default: 'Request Private Appointment'
  assign mf = product.metafields.hartwick

  assign style_name = product.title
  if mf.style.value.display_name != blank
    assign style_name = mf.style.value.display_name
  endif

  assign lot_label = ''
  if mf.lot.value.number_roman != blank
    assign lot_label = 'Lot ' | append: mf.lot.value.number_roman
  endif

  assign form_id = 'HaAppointmentForm'
  assign dialog_id = 'HaAppointmentDialog'
-%}

<div class="ha-pdp__appointment">
  <button
    class="ha-link ha-record ha-appointment__open"
    type="button"
    data-ha-appointment-open
    aria-haspopup="dialog"
    aria-controls="{{ dialog_id }}"
  >{{ label }}</button>
</div>

<dialog class="ha-appointment" id="{{ dialog_id }}" aria-labelledby="{{ dialog_id }}-title">
  <div class="ha-appointment__inner">
    <div class="ha-appointment__head">
      <div>
        {%- if lot_label != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-appointment__eyebrow ha-record">{{ lot_label }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h2 class="ha-appointment__title ha-narrate" id="{{ dialog_id }}-title">{{ label }}</h2>
        <p class="ha-appointment__subject ha-record">
          {{ style_name }}{% if mf.expression != blank %} &middot; {{ mf.expression }}{% endif %}
        </p>
      </div>

      <button
        class="ha-appointment__close"
        type="button"
        data-ha-appointment-close
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
      >{% render 'icon-close' %}</button>
    </div>

    {%- form 'contact', id: form_id, class: 'ha-appointment__form' -%}
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        <p class="ha-appointment__status ha-narrate" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-ha-appointment-status>
          Thank you. Your request has reached the atelier and someone will write to you
          to arrange a time.
        </p>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div class="ha-appointment__status ha-appointment__status--error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-ha-appointment-status>
            <p class="ha-narrate">{{ 'templates.contact.form.error_heading' | t }}</p>
            <ul class="ha-appointment__errors ha-record" role="list">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>{{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}</li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The garment is recorded whether or not the visitor mentions it. These
          are the page's own values, not anything the visitor can mistype.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Enquiry type]" value="Private appointment">
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Style]" value="{{ style_name | escape }}">
        {%- if mf.expression != blank -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Expression]" value="{{ mf.expression | escape }}">
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if lot_label != blank -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Lot]" value="{{ lot_label | escape }}">
        {%- endif -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Product]" value="{{ product.title | escape }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Product URL]" value="{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}">
        {%- comment -%} Filled by ha-appointment.js from the live product form. {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Selected size]" value="" data-ha-appointment-size>
        {%- if settings.ha_appointment_recipient != blank -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[Route to]" value="{{ settings.ha_appointment_recipient | escape }}">
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="ha-appointment__fields">
          <p class="ha-appointment__field">
            <label class="ha-appointment__label ha-record" for="{{ form_id }}-name">Name</label>
            <input
              class="ha-appointment__input"
              id="{{ form_id }}-name"
              type="text"
              name="contact[name]"
              autocomplete="name"
              required
              value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name }}{% endif %}"
            >
          </p>

          <p class="ha-appointment__field">
            <label class="ha-appointment__label ha-record" for="{{ form_id }}-email">Email address</label>
            <input
              class="ha-appointment__input"
              id="{{ form_id }}-email"
              type="email"
              name="contact[email]"
              autocomplete="email"
              autocapitalize="off"
              spellcheck="false"
              required
              aria-required="true"
              {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
              value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email }}{% endif %}"
            >
          </p>

          <p class="ha-appointment__field">
            <label class="ha-appointment__label ha-record" for="{{ form_id }}-phone">Telephone number</label>
            <input
              class="ha-appointment__input"
              id="{{ form_id }}-phone"
              type="tel"
              name="contact[Telephone]"
              autocomplete="tel"
              value="{% if customer %}{{ customer.phone }}{% endif %}"
            >
          </p>

          <p class="ha-appointment__field">
            <label class="ha-appointment__label ha-record" for="{{ form_id }}-when">Preferred date or general availability</label>
            {%- comment -%}
              Deliberately free text, not a date picker. Aloha asked for "preferred
              appointment date OR general availability" — "weekday mornings, from
              late September" is a valid answer and a date input cannot hold it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input
              class="ha-appointment__input"
              id="{{ form_id }}-when"
              type="text"
              name="contact[Preferred date or availability]"
              placeholder="A date, or the days and times that suit you"
            >
          </p>

          <p class="ha-appointment__field">
            <label class="ha-appointment__label ha-record" for="{{ form_id }}-message">Message</label>
            <textarea
              class="ha-appointment__input ha-appointment__textarea"
              id="{{ form_id }}-message"
              name="contact[body]"
              rows="4"
            >{% if form.body %}{{ form.body }}{% endif %}</textarea>
          </p>
        </div>

        <button class="ha-appointment__submit ha-record" type="submit">Send request</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endform -%}
  </div>
</dialog>
